{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "04JH", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-morphisms}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d65cbb431b3a731040d1c92b3ec1ed62d3206e0d439e34a80ea69508bda32054", "source_text": "Recovering morphisms", "source_text_hash": "sha256:8695199e68f7e48f4d4d05f291b6fbcf5fd71cc4e3e274e930fe0482cd9ea543", "unit_id": "tag:04JH:title"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "04JH", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "REF_0001": "\\ref{theorem-fully-faithful}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:feea02d6e71695350117090308bafbeb030a82c9256e2ccde00daf8b539ae030", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIn this section we prove that the rule which associates to a scheme\nits locally ringed small <ACCENT_0001>tale topos is fully faithful in a suitable\nsense, see\nTheorem <REF_0001>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:b085d98e44bba86461dab4291dadbf016580f61b79022fb2fabc9a44931d7716", "unit_id": "tag:04JH:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "04JH", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to Y$", "MATH_0002": "$(f_{small}, f_{small}^\\sharp)$", "MATH_0003": "$f$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{sites-modules-definition-morphism-locally-ringed-topoi}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-morphism-locally-ringed}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:29efa7b2283780a23271b10f24e8500680d4d9cff4a9514e676fb6c1906bf9e5", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:28d3e1332cd2830c2f4dcb245e712fd65133188d44607dd75329a00fc97dd30e", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of schemes.\nThe morphism of ringed sites <MATH_0002>\nassociated to <MATH_0003> is a morphism of locally ringed sites, see\nModules on Sites,\nDefinition <REF_0001>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:91883b02776279bc637118a1c8ec72f7688753ceb9084178c22361e8a73ee8f0", "unit_id": "tag:04I5:statement"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "04JH", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$(X_\\etale, \\mathcal{O}_{X_\\etale})$", "MATH_0002": "$(Y_\\etale, \\mathcal{O}_{Y_\\etale})$", "MATH_0003": "$X_\\etale$", "MATH_0004": "$(f_{small}, f_{small}^\\sharp)$", "MATH_0005": "$p$", "MATH_0006": "$X_\\etale$", "MATH_0007": "$p$", "MATH_0008": "$\\overline{x}$", "MATH_0009": "$X$", "MATH_0010": "$q = f_{small} \\circ p$", "MATH_0011": "$\\overline{y} = f \\circ \\overline{x}$", "MATH_0012": "$Y$", "MATH_0013": "$$\n(\\mathcal{O}_Y)_{\\overline{y}} \\longrightarrow (\\mathcal{O}_X)_{\\overline{x}}\n$$", "MATH_0014": "$a \\in (\\mathcal{O}_Y)_{\\overline{y}}$", "MATH_0015": "$a$", "MATH_0016": "$(V, \\overline{v}, a)$", "MATH_0017": "$V \\to Y$", "MATH_0018": "$\\overline{v} : \\overline{x} \\to V$", "MATH_0019": "$Y$", "MATH_0020": "$a \\in \\mathcal{O}(V)$", "MATH_0021": "$(X \\times_Y V, \\overline{x} \\times \\overline{v}, \\text{pr}_V^\\sharp(a))$", "MATH_0022": "$(\\mathcal{O}_X)_{\\overline{x}}$", "MATH_0023": "$\\text{pr}_V^\\sharp(a)$", "MATH_0024": "$\\kappa(\\overline{x})$", "MATH_0025": "$a$", "MATH_0026": "$\\kappa(\\overline{x})$", "MATH_0027": "$a$", "MATH_0028": "$(\\mathcal{O}_Y)_{\\overline{y}}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-etale-site-locally-ringed}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{theorem-exactness-stalks}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{remarks-enough-points}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{sites-modules-lemma-locally-ringed-morphism}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{lemma-points-small-etale-site}", "REF_0006": "\\ref{lemma-stalk-pullback}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:2d8d276edccd069573a0b123bb1aa9acfc5a5ba76643f89c0bd72d6168699acd", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:7476db0cd2629bcab4a32899d411e52957f21609ddf8b8d1c26a12a18a12055d", "source_text": "Note that the assertion makes sense since we have seen that\n<MATH_0001> and\n<MATH_0002>\nare locally ringed sites, see\nLemma <REF_0001>.\nMoreover, we know that <MATH_0003> has enough points, see\nTheorem <REF_0002>\nand\nRemarks <REF_0003>.\nHence it suffices to prove that <MATH_0004>\nsatisfies condition (3) of\nModules on Sites,\nLemma <REF_0004>.\nTo see this take a point <MATH_0005> of <MATH_0006>. By\nLemma <REF_0005>\n<MATH_0007> corresponds to a geometric point <MATH_0008> of <MATH_0009>.\nBy\nLemma <REF_0006>\nthe point <MATH_0010> corresponds to the\ngeometric point <MATH_0011> of <MATH_0012>.\nHence the assertion we have to prove is that the induced map\nof stalks\n<MATH_0013>\nis a local ring map. Suppose that <MATH_0014>\nis an element of the left hand side which maps to an element of the maximal\nideal of the right hand side. Suppose that <MATH_0015> is the equivalence class\nof a triple <MATH_0016> with <MATH_0017> <ACCENT_0001>tale,\n<MATH_0018> over <MATH_0019>, and <MATH_0020>.\nIt maps to the equivalence class of\n<MATH_0021>\nin the local ring <MATH_0022>. But it is clear that\nbeing in the maximal ideal means that pulling back <MATH_0023>\nto an element of <MATH_0024> gives zero. Hence also pulling back\n<MATH_0025> to <MATH_0026> is zero. Which means that <MATH_0027> lies in the\nmaximal ideal of <MATH_0028>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:4d273c4529206d9fc041ddf37d1fa08c73e1d5049be710bea927d002b3b6051a", "unit_id": "tag:04I5:proof"}
